WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:03.510
- So somebody told me this crazy story.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.050
Did you, 'cause polar bears
are, well the most vicious,

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.240
and I heard that you literally, maybe had

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.680
some alcohol one time-

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.090
- Oh gosh.
- And were running on a beach

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.460
where a polar bear was eating.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.230
- I was in a-
- It feels like a bad idea.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.310
- It was a terrible idea.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.130
It was in a movie with Barry Pepper.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.380
I love, you know, Barry
Pepper, Great Canadian actor.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.610
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.850
- And it was up in, like,
Churchill, Manitoba, I think.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.730
And we were drinking at
the wrap party, I think.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:30.630
God, help me, I think.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.092
- All of this says, I think.

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:32.925
- I think.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.400
And then I think in the moment

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.027
we're like, "You know what we should do?

00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:38.970
"We should, like, race down the beach."

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.910
And so me and him and another guy came,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.380
we came running down this beach

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.980
and a guy that lived there
just started swearing.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.020
Literally swearing at
us and just screaming.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.000
I mean screaming bloody murder.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.833
- Buzzkill.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:52.800
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.920
But 'cause we didn't
realize we were running

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.051
to our certain death

00:00:57.051 --> 00:00:57.884
(audience laughing)

00:00:57.884 --> 00:00:59.820
because there were polar
bears all down the beach.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.500
And yes, they're the most aggressive.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.428
God, but they're so cuddly.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:03.310
- They're beautiful.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.142
(audience laughing) Yeah.
- Yeah, but they will eat you.

00:01:05.142 --> 00:01:06.690
- In those Coca-Cola commercials-

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.677
- Yes.
- You're like snuggle, yeah.

00:01:07.677 --> 00:01:09.510
- And so that is true, I did that.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.670
Like, sometimes I wonder about that,

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.760
how close I was to being, like,
a little polar bear lunch.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.080
- Yeah, well who would've thought

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:16.980
they were just polar bears?

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.367
Nobody ever hears that,

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.920
"Oh, there's polar bears
hanging on the beach."

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.150
It just doesn't happen.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.410
- Well, yeah, up there was amazing.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.300
We used to rent these little zodiacs.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.133
- Yeah.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.170
- Oh my god, why can't
I remember his name?

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.380
He's such a beautiful human
being: James Cromwell.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.580
- Yeah.
- Remember James Cromwell?

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.410
He's such a wonderful character actor.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.090
You might remember him from "Babe",

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.350
remember, "That'll do pig."

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.250
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah
- [Audience] Yeah.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.508
- And he and I used to go and, yes.

00:01:40.508 --> 00:01:41.341
(Michael, Kelly and audience applauding)

00:01:41.341 --> 00:01:45.974
- Give it up, give it up.

00:01:45.974 --> 00:01:47.370
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:48.203
- I'm trying to know,

00:01:48.203 --> 00:01:49.680
are we clapping for James or the pig?

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.617
- The pig.

00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.283
"That'll do."
- Or just that I remember,

00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:53.116
"That'll do pig"?
- All of the things,

00:01:53.116 --> 00:01:54.295
we're just happy in the new year.

00:01:54.295 --> 00:01:55.170
(Kelly chuckling)

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.030
- But we used to, it was like 40 bucks

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.370
and we would go and
rent a zodiac and go out

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.440
and all these little beluga
whales would follow us,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.490
Good times.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.194
- [Audience] Aw!
- Oh, that's beautiful, yeah.

00:02:04.194 --> 00:02:05.780
(audience laughing)

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.720
- You know, let's move on.
- No, that's beautiful.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.670
It's important for me
to get out of the city

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.630
and experience stuff like that

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:10.520
for my, like, emotional state.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.610
- Oh, it's so cool.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.020
Everyone in your audience,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.920
almost everyone, literally at
the same time just went, "Aw"-

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.330
- Yeah.
- Except one dude,

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.323
right there.

00:02:19.323 --> 00:02:20.790
(audience laughing)
(Kelly clapping)

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:21.623
- Calling you out.
- That was you,

00:02:21.623 --> 00:02:23.670
in the beautiful gray: good looking dude.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.710
And he did this, like this.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.863
- [Kelly] He's like, that
sounds horrible, man.

